{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and actuation capabilities as separate automata. The specification encodes safe, efficient exploration: random_walk is used in clear/search states, move_forward is used for short progress, and obstacle events trigger conservative, one-shot recovery turns. Forward is never enabled when an obstacle is detected. Recovery states are deterministic and only allow a single turn or scan action before returning to exploration. All uncontrollable events are handled in every state, and the supervisor is never allowed to stall.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception and motion to reflect the robot's hardware modularity.",
    "Specification automaton encodes the safe exploration policy: random_walk in clear, move_forward in progress, deterministic recovery turns on obstacle, and rapid return to exploration after recovery."
  ],
